**Lemma 10.1 (complete rational source implications).** The inherited source box implies

$$
1/4<r_T<2/5,\qquad 1/10<r_S<1/6,\qquad
7/10<h_1/h_0<3/4,\qquad4/5<h_2/h_0<5/6.
\tag{PG.48}
$$

All twelve original Grams are real positive definite.

Proof. The following is the RG rational implication chain, retained as inherited credit rather than a new root certificate. Put
$r_5^{\rm src}=1+\alpha_1^2+\alpha_2^2$ and
$r_{27}^{\rm src}=1+\beta_1^2+\beta_2^2$.
The box and positive square comparisons give

$$
\begin{gathered}
.479<\lambda_{\rm src}<.480,\quad
1.412<\alpha_1<1.413,\quad1.185<\alpha_2<1.186,\quad
.413<\beta_1<.414,\quad .809<\beta_2<.810,\quad\eta_1>.19,\\
4.39<r_5^{\rm src}<4.41,\quad1.82<r_{27}^{\rm src}<1.83,\quad
2.23<\sqrt5<2.24,\quad5.19<\sqrt{27}<5.20,\quad
17<\sqrt{295}<18,\quad31<\sqrt{999}<32.
\end{gathered}
\tag{PG.49}
$$

For example the first two denominator bounds follow by squaring the chart endpoints and adding one; radical bounds follow by squaring positive rational endpoints. Positive numerator/denominator bounds in (PG.4) give

$$
\begin{aligned}
(A_5^{\rm src})_{00}&>\frac{(.479)(1.412)^2}{4.41}>.21,&
(A_{27}^{\rm src})_{00}&>\frac{(.520)(.413)^2}{1.83}>.04,\\
.180&<\frac{(.479)(1.412)(1.185)}{4.41}
 <(A_5^{\rm src})_{01}
 <\frac{(.480)(1.413)(1.186)}{4.39}<.185,\\
.094&<\frac{(.520)(.413)(.809)}{1.83}
 <(A_{27}^{\rm src})_{01}
 <\frac{(.521)(.414)(.810)}{1.82}<.097.
\end{aligned}
\tag{PG.50}
$$

Hence

$$
.045<\frac{180\cdot17+94\cdot31}{128000}
 <N^{\rm src}_{01}
 =\frac{(A_5^{\rm src})_{01}\sqrt{295}+
         (A_{27}^{\rm src})_{01}\sqrt{999}}{128}
 <\frac{185\cdot18+97\cdot32}{128000}<.051.
\tag{PG.51}
$$

Retain the sign in the other off-diagonal source entry:
$N^{\rm src}_{02}=P_{\rm pos}-P_{\rm neg}$, with

$$
\begin{aligned}
.021&<\frac{(.479)(1.412)(2.23)}{16(4.41)}
 <P_{\rm neg}=\frac{\lambda_{\rm src}\alpha_1\sqrt5}{16r_5^{\rm src}}
 <\frac{(.480)(1.413)(2.24)}{16(4.39)}<.022,\\
.038&<\frac{(.520)(.413)(5.19)}{16(1.83)}
 <P_{\rm pos}=\frac{(1-\lambda_{\rm src})\beta_1\sqrt{27}}{16r_{27}^{\rm src}}
