In particular $a/b<.51,c/d<.18$, which also prove the failure margins used in Section 2 as explained there.

For $a_y$ all coordinates are positive. Its only potential positive singular height, by (PG.23), is

$$
y_{\rm crit}=\frac{64(r_T+r_S)}{1+r_T}.
$$

The inequalities
$48r_T+64r_S>48/4+64/10>16$ and
$37r_T+64r_S<37(2/5)+64/6<27$
give $16<y_{\rm crit}<27$. None of $5,16,27$ equals it. The three output columns are therefore independent, and the Gram is positive definite. Sign congruence below proves all four signs at each height. $\square$

